Z||000004||BC-GT||07-18-2001||08:29 PM||||What exactly has to be cut away from the block when doing an automatic conversion? Any pics out there? Finally found someone here in Vancouver who will do one for me and then he backs away when he finds out it's an auto :-(<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||07-19-2001||02:09 AM||||Darryl, a slight bit of the lower flange of the block (opposite where the new starter mounting is made) needs to be ground off to clear the automatic tranny - it is not a major problem to do and can be done with a hand grinder..........||||reg||1
